 34AR c  {+36}Ar|)2n+{+34}Ar from J|p=0+ {+36}Ar ground state.                  
 34AR c  2018Lo11: a 100-MeV proton beam was produced from the RCNP WS beam     
 34AR2c  line. The target was 0.76-mg/cm{+2} enriched {+36}Ar gas (|>99%).      
 34AR3c  Reaction products were momentum-analyzed by the Grand Raiden           
 34AR4c  spectrograph and detected using the focal-plane detector system.       
 34AR5c  Measured |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced levels. Calculated astrophysical        
 34AR6c  {+30}S(|a,p){+33}Cl reaction rate. Also see 2009ObZY.                  
 34AR c  1972Pa02: 40-45-MeV proton beams were produced from the MSU            
 34AR2c  sector-focused cyclotron. The target was >99%-enriched {+36}Ar gas.    
 34AR3c  Reaction products were detected using a detector telescope made up of  
 34AR4c  two silicon surface-barrier transmission mounted counters. Measured    
 34AR5c  |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, and |p from JULIE-DWBA   
 34AR6c  analysis.                                                              
 34AR c  1969Br21: a 45-MeV proton beam was produced from the Berkeley 88-Inch  
 34AR2c  Cyclotron. The target was 99.6%-enriched {+36}Ar gas. Reaction products
 34AR3c  were detected using 155-|um phosphorus-diffused silicon |DE            
 34AR4c  transmission counter and 3.0-mm lithium-drifted silicon E counter      
 34AR5c  operated in coincidence, followed by a 0.5-mm lithium-drifted silicon  
 34AR6c  E-reject counter operated in anti-coincidence with the first two       
 34AR7c  counters to eliminate long-range particles. Measured |s(E{-t},|q).     
 34AR8c  Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, and |p from DWUCK-DWBA analysis.       
 34AR9c  Compared with {+36}Ar(p,{+3}He){+34}Cl and {+36}Ar(d,|a){+34}Cl data.  
 34AR c  Other:                                                                 
 34AR c  1974Ha02: E=40.2 MeV. Measured Q value. Tritons for the g.s. to g.s.   
 34AR2c  transition measured using split-pole magnetic spectrograph, FWHM=10-25 
 34AR3c  keV. Measures Q value=-19513 {I3}, deduced mass excess                 
